#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "092a29e0-d74d-5d43-953c-1f5d9bf2a5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388295} {:answer/id #uuid "60cc9f6b-b572-50b9-952f-12e386a01c9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388296} {:answer/id #uuid "aea1d3dc-a5bf-519d-8f6d-ded54403dbfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388297} {:answer/id #uuid "133a0e32-0ea5-5f11-8c08-78665b249cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388298} {:answer/id #uuid "81d539a4-fe56-54af-a346-d28ee3e104cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "092a29e0-d74d-5d43-953c-1f5d9bf2a5a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388295} :answer-field/id #uuid "66942a40-bd6e-5606-91e2-d8c0f63814d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9a7843d-3020-5482-8aef-e872811d9165" :question/math-academy-id "q-132565" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1-e}^{0}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{e-1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/34/3426e7bdd134bc9af5a3665f8c9c55a65514afa9dca5be112eabb37479c4c9ec.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,1-e\\le y\\le 0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)\\le x\\le 1}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le e-1,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\le x\\le 1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)\\,⟹\\,y={e}^{x}-1,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)\\,⟹\\,y=1-{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-{e}^{x}\\le y\\le {e}^{x}-1},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/7d/7d88d351b481859ec3e77350d3679387836d2e7f67325caca50e2f61cce9dcce.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1-e}^{0}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-y)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{e-1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{e}^{x}}^{{e}^{x}-1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129190 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" :knowledge-point/title "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Partitioned Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13af14b5-15a1-566b-a656-d8a378d7320c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324147} {:answer/id #uuid "1d1a2f03-596f-5e6f-978b-605dcec2e3eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324215} {:answer/id #uuid "860bc5a9-e2eb-5f7c-a636-43aba8e0881d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{4-y}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325106} {:answer/id #uuid "a0fec665-57db-5f83-bb6e-f9267a2d10aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4-y}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325336} {:answer/id #uuid "f2804b9b-bae3-55b0-8ce1-7ac7c4d428a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2804b9b-bae3-55b0-8ce1-7ac7c4d428a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326107} :answer-field/id #uuid "759c1086-e737-5e21-a10a-cebde7f9cab4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "51957ec1-4df6-5139-b864-fabbb3776e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-38601" :question/problem "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ea/ea36f1ec1ddeb03dd8d133fb8d65b5d50b3fa07ba34495978d87f95742dee042.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type I regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le x}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny=x\\,⟹\\,x=y\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-x\\,⟹\\,x=4-y.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y\\le x\\le 4-y},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/e8/e82098a4bb63f1d709a06b6a24da078594716d6a3cc0fa2e069af9dcd9154955.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y}^{4-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
